removed_case_id tower kay g 48 f  reg ref removed_date    removed_case_id  wic schroeder david m d                                                                                             specimen  removed_accession_id removed_case_id sout received  removed_date  1450 spec type    clinical diagnosis   history  focal calcifications seen on mammography  benign vs  malignant calcifications edited by  removed_date    1459 pat dord gross description  the specimen is received in formalin in one container  labeled  stereotactic breast biopsy  left breast calcification  designated  left breast lower central  and contains a purple cassette which contains two firm  reddish pink  glistening needle biopsies measuring removed_date cm  in length  removed_date cm  in diameter and removed_date cm  in length  removed_date cm  in diameter  resubmitted in cassette removed_date x all  also present within the container are seven firm  yellowish pink  glistening needle biopsies ranging in size from removed_date cm  in length x removed_date cm  in diameter to removed_date cm  in length x removed_date cm  in diameter  submitted in cassettes removed_date  7x all  dictated by  lv edited by  removed_date    1459 pat dord diagnosis  left breast  lower central  needle biopsy  atypical columnar cell lesion  atypical ductal hyperplasia  columnar cell type  with microcalcifications  final diagnosis by  michael j  ross  m d  edited by  removed_date    1609 pat dord notes  removed_date  all seven slides ret d from mgh  jam  removed_accession_id  removed_date  dr  koerner s report rec d via fax  djd removed_date  sent seven slides  1 1l 3l  removed_date l 3l and removed_date l 3l  to dr  frederick koerner   mgh via courier for opinion mjr jam  removed_accession_id   617  removed_date  23 06  all six slides and report ret d from bi deac med center  jam  cr  removed_date  per patient  sent 6 slides to b i deac   dr  valerie staradub  5th floor  att  lauren removed_date  labeled  1 2l  removed_date l  removed_date l  removed_date l  removed_date l  removed_date l  mjr dg co notes   continued  edited by  removed_date    1130 pat gild removed_date    1103 pat murj removed_date    1105 pat murj removed_date    0912 pat murj removed_date    1010 pat dord removed_date    1001 pat murj addendum reportaddendum  1 entered  removed_date  1304     additional diagnostic information     this report contains an addendum to the original for the purpose of providing additional diagnostic information  the original diagnosis is unchanged  this case has been reviewed by dr  frederick koerner  of the massachusetts general hospital  who concurs with the diagnosis  he comments   i agree wholeheartedly with your analysis of this case  the sections of this core biopsy specimen show a background of slight fibrocystic changes  a population of atypical ductal cells occupies the acini of several terminal duct lobular units in block  1   the cells appear enlarged and they possess slightly enlarged nuclei  homogeneous chromatin  inconspicuous nucleoli  and modest amounts of eosinophilic  apical cytoplasm  the cells grow in a single  crowded layer  they do not show genuine stratification nor do they form cribriform spaces  trabecular bars  or roman bridges  like you  i would classify the proliferation as atypical ductal hyperplasia of columnar cell type  i suspect that the atypical cells represent a neoplastic proliferation  but i cannot exclude the possibility that they constitute an unusual form of ductal hyperplasia  an excision of this region of the patient s left breast would probably clarify this uncertainty  addendum final  ross michael j  m d    removed_date   04 04 06 1407  by md rosmj edited by  removed_date    1304 pat murjcodes  removed_accession_id   left breast  no removed_accession_id   left breast  no atypical removed_accession_id   columnar epithe removed_accession_id   columnar epithe lesion  nos removed_accession_id   columnar epithe atypical hyperp removed_accession_id  