removed_case_id fiske kathleen a 61 f  reg ref removed_date    removed_case_id  wic skornik ronee a  m d                                                                                             specimen  removed_accession_id removed_case_id sout received  removed_date  1123 spec type    clinical diagnosis   history  8 mm  cluster of indeterminate microcalcifications of left lower inner breast  tiny cluster of calcifications left breast    ductal carcinoma in situ versus fibrocystic changes edited by  removed_date    1128 pat gild gross description  the specimen is received in formalin in one container  labeled  stereotactic breast biopsy  left breast calcifications  and is contained in two cassettes  the first cassette is purple and designated  left lower inner quadrant with calcifications  and consists of a 2 x removed_date x removed_date cm  aggregate of yellowish pink  firm needle biopsies each measuring removed_date cm  in diameter  submitted in cassette removed_date agg  all  the second cassette is aqua in color  designated to container  the remainder of the tissue  consists of a removed_date x 2 x removed_date cm  aggregate of yellowish pink  firm needle biopsies each measuring removed_date cm  in diameter  submitted in cassette removed_date agg  all  dictated by  lv edited by  removed_date    1128 pat gild diagnosis  left breast  lower inner quadrant  needle core biopsies  microcalcifications identified and associated with atypical ductal hyperplasia  see note   edited by  removed_date    1317 pat gild removed_date    1203 pat murj descriptive comment  note  this case was sent to dr  frederick koerner at massachusetts general hospital  he concurs with the above diagnosis of atypical ductal hyperplasia  he adds   i agree with those in your department who favor the diagnosis of atypical ductal hyperplasia and i believe that the region of slide  1 1l  marked with red and blue demonstrates the atypicality most clearly  a population of atypical ductal cells fills and distends a small duct  they appear slightly enlarged and they possess ample  eosinophilic cytoplasm and nuclei containing homogeneous chromatin  atypical columnar cells growing in a single layer and forming stubby small papillae distend a collection of glands  but distortion of the tissue makes it difficult to evaluate this focus  i acknowledge that the degree of proliferation in these areas seem slight and the nature of the cytological atypicality subtle  nevertheless  i would urge the patient and her physicians to consider an excision of this region of the left breast  examination of a larger sample would provide a more secure evaluation of the extent and the significance of the atypical ductal hyperplasia   final diagnosis by  nicole a  mihok  m d  edited by  removed_date    1208 pat murj notes  removed_date  received all 6 slides and report from mgh via mail  nam mi  cr  removed_date  rec d mgh path report via fax  dg removed_date  report faxed from mgh  jam removed_date  per nam  sent for opinion to mgh  dr  koerner  sent  6  slides labeled  1 1l 3l  removed_date l 3l  nam dg co edited by  removed_date    0914 pat gild removed_date    1120 pat murj removed_date    0733 pat gild removed_date    1044 pat indmcodes  removed_accession_id   left breast  no needle breanbx removed_accession_id    breanbx atypical hyperp edited by  removed_date    1317 pat gild removed_date    1203 pat murjcopies to  selland donna lee m d  newton wellesley radiology newton  ma removed_case_id  617 243 6600 skornik ronee a  m d  173 worcester st  wellesley  ma removed_case_id  781 237 0080markers  breast disease related  presented at breast ca conf   consult case out  consult case return edited by  removed_date    1128 pat gild removed_date    0913 pat gild removed_date    1044 pat indm removed_date    1100 pat murjprocedures  removed_accession_id  05 18 05 1317 pat gild  edited by  removed_date    1128 pat gild removed_date    1317 pat gild removed_date    1208 pat murjtissues  